Here's a summary of everything changed in this round:

**`BitmapTransformation.java`** — Replaced a 6-line assign-then-return pattern with a single ternary return in `transform()`.

**`LogTime.java`** — Extracted the repeated `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= JELLY_BEAN_MR1` check into a named constant `USE_REALTIME_NANOS`, eliminating the duplicate evaluation.

**`LruBitmapPool.java`** — Collapsed `getDefaultStrategy()`'s assign-once-then-return into a direct ternary return.

**`LruResourceCache.java`** — Removed the redundant `else` branch after an early `return` in `getSize()`.

**`ExceptionCatchingInputStream.java`** — Eliminated assign-once local variables in all four I/O overrides (`read()`, `read(buffer)`, `read(buffer,off,count)`, `skip()`) by returning directly from try/catch.

**`Downsampler.java`** — Replaced the double `options.get(ALLOW_HARDWARE_CONFIG)` call (null-check then re-fetch) with `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`.

**`HttpUrlFetcher.java`** — Removed a redundant `else` block after a `throw` in `loadDataWithRedirects()`.

**`ByteBufferUtil.java`** — Removed a redundant `else` block after an early `return`.

